            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0484" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/2054: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Arica</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Von Tresckow</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-03-26T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                                1926—10 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Lassiter. Your telegram March 25, 3 p.m., received. I wholly approve position
                    you took in proceedings yesterday and think that the formal record at this time
                    is satisfactory. I shall send further suggestions, especially with regard to the
                    resolution for the suspension of proceedings, as soon as replies have been
                    received from Santiago and Lima, as stated in my telegram of March 25, 6
                        p.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d203-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
